meta {
  name: Decide - Task search
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{opaUrl}}/v1/data/umzh/authz/gateway/allow
  body: json
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "input": {
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/fhir/Task",
        "query": {},
        "headers": {
          "authorization": "Bearer {{bearerToken}}"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

docs {
  An external consumer (a gateway / integration platform, e.g. MuleSoft) asks OPA:
  may this caller run GET /fhir/Task? Pass the request being proxied
  (method/path/query) + the client's bearer. OPA decodes scope/org/fhirContext
  from the token and injects fhir_base from its OWN config — you pass NEITHER.
  Response: { "result": true|false }. (Allows when the token carries system/Task.s
  — or the combined system/Task.crus — and a non-empty org.)
}
